#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Nightly quality run for raft-flutter (machine-local, scheduled by cron).

Four jobs on a fresh worktree of origin/cindy/integration, one Chinese summary:

  1. coverage   the app suite (plus raft_ui / raft_client / raft_sync package suites) with
                `--coverage`, a per-area summary, and a diff-coverage report for every open PR
                against cindy/integration: its changed executable lines that no test ran. The PR's own
                tree is tested (only the test files that can reach a changed file, tool/affected_tests.py),
                results are cached per (PR, head, merge-base).
  2. osv        osv-scanner over every pubspec.lock, and the list of dependency inputs it cannot see.
  3. random     the app suite runs in a random order (--test-randomize-ordering-seed); the seed is recorded
                so a failure reproduces. Job 1 and job 3 are the same app run: coverage does not depend on
                order, and a second 25 minute run would only repeat it.
  3b. legacy-looks  the Dart tests of the legacy looks (Elegant, Brutal) and the theme engine package, through
                `tool/theme-suite --look all --tests-only`: the Raft run above tests the Raft look only. Its coverage joins job 1.
  4. visual     the fast subset of the three-level visual suite (tool/nightly_visual.py): L1 frame cases and
                the key L2 pages at phone and desktop widths, light mode, for the Raft look (against the Web
                v1.21.23 render) and the Elegant / Brutal looks (against their frozen a57b9dab originals); the
                summary lists the cases below the 96% line and every drop since the previous night.

The test jobs take the shared gate lock (/tmp/raft-flutter-check.lock, same flock as tool/prepare-handoff)
so they never overlap a gate; they wait up to --lock-wait-minutes and then record "skipped: gate busy".
Everything is bounded: per-run timeouts, a PR budget, and a total deadline (--max-hours).
Nothing is committed or pushed; flutter's temp dirs live under a private TMPDIR that is removed at the end.

Output: ~/.local/share/raft-nightly/<date>/summary.md (+ summary.json, per-job logs, lcov files).
Usage:  tool/nightly-quality [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--seed N] [--lock-wait-minutes M] [--max-prs N] [--no-gate-lock]
                             [--app-tests PATH ...] [--skip-packages] [--skip-prs] [--skip-osv] [--skip-visual]
"""
